        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): add Wear conversations, voice, agents, and sessions",
        "body": "[AI-assisted]\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's Android node keeps the authenticated Gateway connection on the phone, leaving Wear OS users without a safe wrist interface for the active conversation, voice prompts, sessions, available agents, and reply playback.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change adds the OpenClaw Wear OS interaction surface while keeping the Android phone as the transport and security boundary. The branch now uses the shared `WearProtocol` introduced on current `main` by #108835 and implements only its allowlisted `proxy.status`, `sessions.list`, `chat.history`, `chat.send`, and `chat.abort` methods.\n\nThe paired phone proxies bounded snapshots and actions through its existing authenticated `NodeRuntime`. The watch receives no Gateway token, password, endpoint, direct identity, or raw session key. The previous duplicate status and conversation envelopes were removed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpenClaw Wear OS provides four swipeable Chat, Agents, Sessions, and Controls pages. Users can submit prompts with Talk or Type, follow the active transcript and response state, switch sessions, inspect agents available on the paired phone, hear replies through watch TTS, enable automatic reply speech, and persist Dark or Light appearance.\n\nThe Wear artifact now has its own Play-safe version-code scheme, a signed AAB/APK release path, release metadata and certificate validation, Wear OS branding, module CI gates, and third-party license notices.\n\n## Evidence\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ### Validation\n>\n> - [x] Current upstream `main` merged through `63b0cac9f0`; pushed head is `31d678bd93`.\n> - [x] `./gradlew :wear-shared:testDebugUnitTest :wear:testDebugUnitTest :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest :app:assemblePlayDebug :wear:assembleDebug :wear:lintDebug :wear-shared:lintDebug :app:ktlintCheck :wear:ktlintCheck :wear-shared:ktlintCheck` — passed.\n> - [x] `test/scripts/android-release-artifacts.test.ts` — 14/14 tests passed.\n> - [x] Targeted Android CI workflow-contract guard — passed.\n> - [x] `native:i18n:check` — passed after synchronizing the moved Wear source IDs across the native inventory and all 21 locale artifacts without changing translation text.\n> - [x] `:wear:bundleRelease` and `:wear:assembleRelease` — passed locally with the standard Android debug key as a non-production proof identity.\n> - [x] Wear AAB verification — `jar verified.`, not unsigned.\n> - [x] Phone and Wear use package `ai.openclaw.app`, versionName `2026.7.2`, and the same local proof certificate `58e48afd…55a6d371`.\n> - [x] Phone versionCode `2026070201`; Wear versionCode `260702011`.\n> - [x] Wear release APK manifest: `ai.openclaw.app` / `2026.7.2` / `260702011`.\n> - [x] Windows APK validation starts `apksigner.jar` directly through Java without a shell boundary and accepts current scheme-prefixed certificate output.\n> - [x] `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` — passed.\n> - [ ] GitHub CI is running on pushed head `31d678bd93`.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> ### Real Behavior Proof\n>\n> Physical Android device proof uses a paired Pixel phone and Samsung Galaxy Watch with the 480×480 Wear OS UI.\n>\n> - [x] **UI walkthrough:** Chat, Agents, Sessions, Controls, Dark/Light switching, and return navigation are visible on the physical watch.\n> - [x] **Conversation result:** The Chat page shows the active session, submitted prompt, and returned agent response.\n> - [x] **Security boundary:** The paired phone owns Gateway authentication and transport; the watch uses Wear Data Layer only.\n> - [x] **Persistence surface:** Appearance and automatic reply-speech controls are exposed on the watch.\n> - [x] **Exact-head install:** Phone and watch proof APKs from pushed head `31d678bd93` are installed.\n> - [x] **Microphone proof:** A watch voice prompt is recognized and delivered to the active session.\n> - [x] **TTS proof:** The agent reply is played audibly through watch TTS.\n>\n> The operator-attested physical proof completes the exact-head install, watch microphone recognition, prompt delivery, and audible TTS playback checks.\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th>Chat, Talk, and Type</th><th>Agents view</th></tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IWhatsskill/openclaw/5d27bcc19807b3b29c63dc94deff8827bd94fe65/docs/images/openclaw-watchos-conversation.jpg\" alt=\"OpenClaw Wear OS Chat page showing ready state, Talk and Type controls, and the active conversation\" /></td>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IWhatsskill/openclaw/5d27bcc19807b3b29c63dc94deff8827bd94fe65/docs/images/openclaw-watchos-agents.jpg\" alt=\"OpenClaw Wear OS Agents page showing agents available through the paired phone\" /></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\nComplete physical-watch walkthrough — Chat, Agents, Sessions, Controls, and appearance settings:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1faa6be3-fdc0-4f18-8f85-806bc95fb298\n\nExact-head Voice and TTS proof — watch microphone recognition, prompt delivery, and audible reply playback (operator-attested):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2bc1fbd0-e738-4e72-ad5f-e98adb557c69\n",
