        "locked": false,
        "title": "[Bug] Destructive Formatting in sanitizeForPromptLiteral Strips Tabs and Newlines",
        "body": "### Summary / Problem Statement\nIn `src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.ts`, `sanitizeForPromptLiteral` uses a broad regular expression to match Unicode control characters (`Cc`). This regex inadvertently strips tabs (`\\t`) and newlines (`\\n`), destroying code indentation and layout alignment before forwarding the payload to the LLM.\n\n### Detailed Technical Context\n- **Vulnerable Code Location:** [src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.ts](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.ts#L19)\n- **Mechanics:**\n  ```typescript\n  const CcPattern = /[\\p{Cc}\\p{Cf}\\u2028\\u2029]/gu;\n  return input.replace(CcPattern, \"\");\n  ```\n- The category `\\p{Cc}` matches all control characters, including tabs and newlines, destroying code block structure.\n\n### Impact Analysis\n- Loss of code indentation in prompt injections, causing degraded LLM code understanding.\n- Failure of code-related operations (like syntax analysis) that depend on correct indentation.\n\n### Proposed Solution\n1. Exclude tab (`\\u0009`) and newline (`\\u000A`, `\\u000D`) characters from the sanitization pattern.\n\n### Affected File References\n- [sanitize-for-prompt.ts:L10-L25](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.ts#L10-L25)",
